{"kind":"assert","text":"# AE-1 retained capacity numbers\n\nRead-only report for rulings `da80156910a5abb4383b623ef3a3dce7992d5e3e` and `2df54f2d5fe19ff035f659c356f8b3b594cb4a1f`. No project code ran for this report. No source, observer, cap, charge, assertion or deadline changed. The diagnostic branch stays closed; Grow diagnostic and generous passes remain held. These numbers establish neither a minimum nor acceptance.\n\nThe failed Base target is the **application child, seq 1**. Its refused finish requires one node beyond the original cap. The shared Grow producer is the **application root, seq 0**. Its refused finish requires 8,593,773 input-work units beyond the original cap. Both ordinary executions at exact `ca1efcea0b1b8ca9c0aa6b0a0de83e9db36600bd` print the same seven vectors below. No time finding follows.\n\n## Six Base blocks\n\nVector order throughout: **entries, attempts, nodes, calls, metadata, inputWork**. Original caps are **[4096,512,64,16384,4194304,67108864]**, with the original 30-second allowance (`packages/scope/src/archive-budget.ts:7–8` at ca1).\n\nThe confirmed rows report **terminal used**. The refused row reports used **before the refused affordability call**; `canSpend` spends nothing (`archive-budget.ts:77–86`). A bold coordinate reaches at least 90% of its cap. No unmarked coordinate reaches that threshold.\n\n| Record / scope | Seq | Decision | Used vector | Refused request | At least 90% of cap |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| records[0], application root | 0 | confirmed | [2,48,37,182,1233583,47444983] | None; capacityRefusal is null | None |\n| records[0], application root | 1 | confirmed | [2,94,**58**,253,1317911,39779349] | None; capacityRefusal is null | Used nodes 58/64 = **90.625%** |\n| records[0], application root | 2 | confirmed | [2,81,**61**,247,1284115,39033545] | None; capacityRefusal is null | Used nodes 61/64 = **95.3125%** |\n| records[0], application root | 3 | confirmed | [2,71,55,212,1174883,33644707] | None; capacityRefusal is null | None |\n| records[1], application child | 0 | confirmed | [2,28,39,159,1154242,44832419] | None; capacityRefusal is null | None |\n| records[1], application child | 1 | retry / limit | [1,33,35,114,845935,26259250] | [1,56,30,148,1026672,16483384] | Used: none. Projected nodes **65/64 = 101.5625%** |\n\nThe ordinary loop takes each record, then each sealed entry, and checks confirmation immediately (`archive-installed.fixture.ts:616–621`). Eligible order is [root,child,D,A,G] (:541–544). The child's failure prevents the D/A/G passes. A confirmed pass has **no refused request**; its successful finish quote and its used vector immediately before that successful quote are not printed. This report does not replace those missing values with zero.\n\nOriginal END755 stdout block lines: **13105,13208,13311,13414,13517,13620**. Replay stdout block lines: **2827,2930,3033,3136,3239,3342**. Source attribution is recorded separately in `scope-attribution-correction.md`; the two diagnostic branches selected root seq 1, an earlier successful ordinary pass, rather than the failed child seq 1. No selector repair or rerun follows.\n\n## Refused target dimensions\n\nBoth refusals have `kind: finish-quote`, `site: finish-affordability`, zero protected/reserved coordinates, and zero unsettled metadata. `sourceFailure` is null. `archive-adaptive.ts:162` constructs the forecast; :169–173 checks affordability. The request is a forecast of remaining work, not an actual debit. Projected means **used + request**; shortfall means **max(0, projected − cap)** (`archive-budget.ts:91–105`). Percentages below distinguish final/pre-call used from projected work.\n\n### Base application child, seq 1\n\n| Dimension | Used before call | Request | Cap | Projected | Shortfall | Used / cap | Projected / cap |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| entries | 1 | 1 | 4096 | 2 | 0 | 0.024414% | 0.048828% |\n| attempts | 33 | 56 | 512 | 89 | 0 | 6.445313% | 17.382813% |\n| nodes | 35 | 30 | 64 | **65** | **1** | 54.687500% | **101.562500%** |\n| calls | 114 | 148 | 16384 | 262 | 0 | 0.695801% | 1.599121% |\n| metadata | 845935 | 1026672 | 4194304 | 1872607 | 0 | 20.168662% | 44.646430% |\n| inputWork | 26259250 | 16483384 | 67108864 | 42742634 | 0 | 39.129332% | 63.691488% |\n\n### Shared Grow producer root, seq 0\n\n| Dimension | Used before call | Request | Cap | Projected | Shortfall | Used / cap | Projected / cap |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| entries | 1 | 1 | 4096 | 2 | 0 | 0.024414% | 0.048828% |\n| attempts | 14 | 34 | 512 | 48 | 0 | 2.734375% | 9.375000% |\n| nodes | 21 | 18 | 64 | 39 | 0 | 32.812500% | 60.937500% |\n| calls | 76 | 105 | 16384 | 181 | 0 | 0.463867% | 1.104736% |\n| metadata | 873441 | 1050377 | 4194304 | 1923818 | 0 | 20.824456% | 45.867395% |\n| inputWork | 45969870 | 29732767 | 67108864 | **75702637** | **8593773** | 68.500444% | **112.805720%** |\n\nOriginal Grow block starts at stdout line **13962**; replay starts at **3684**. Both producers fail before their genuine clone/replay/accepted-answer checks can complete. Their two command followers then fail because the producer did not retain its handoff; those followers are not two additional measured budget shortages.\n\n## The audit's exact five parts\n\nThe retained prior list is `notes/implementation/2026-11-14-ae1-shared-archive.md:199–209` in the ca31 AE1 checkout. It names five **variable pre-entry components**, not five disjoint numeric pieces of the refused quote. The following mapping preserves that distinction. Source references below use exact ca1 unless stated otherwise.\n\n| Prior audit part | Already spent before this quote | Included in remaining finish request / unknown |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Target discovery and initial format/target persistence, including actual mutable Directory/Destination reply sizes | `archive-driver.ts:241–257`, `archive-target.ts:64–88`, and `apps/room/archive.ts:55,65–84` charge discovery/admission; an absent row also needs initial persistence. | No separate target-discovery term in the request. Discovered format/scopes/source context affect publication and patch forecasts (`archive-finish-cost.ts:53–78`). Actual reply sizes and per-operation debits are not printed. |\n| 2. Warm policy/release/prepared/owned table sizes, which determine reset work | `apps/room/archive-packages.ts:127–130` charges reset sizes before clearing/restoring native policies; :65–67 charges declaration validation and population. Formulas: `archive-setup-cost.ts:27–29`. | No warm-table-size argument enters the finish request. Fresh inventory/source admission grants no credit for earlier policy validation. Actual table sizes and their separate debit vectors are not printed. |\n| 3. Current trust text length, row count, and repeated provider comparisons | `archive-packages.ts:31–55` pays comparisons and parsing as needed; :62,69 checks trust around declaration validation. Formulas: `archive-setup-cost.ts:19–23`. | No explicit trust text/count/multiplicity term enters `forecastArchiveFinish`. Later provider checks still call policyCurrent (`archive-driver.ts:174`), so the quote does not establish that all future trust work has already been spent or numerically forecast. Actual units/counts/check multiplicity are not printed. |\n| 4. Retained archive row, manifests, confirmed frontier, and current parent | Row load/validation (`archive-row.ts:155–169`), frontier reads (`archive-frontier-store.ts:134–166`), parent basis (`archive-driver.ts:310–344`) and parent/layout preparation (`journal-v2-preparation.ts:39–58,94–126`) spend work before affordability. `archive-finish-cost.ts:30–38` also spends parent-descriptor work before returning the forecast. | Future bookkeeping uses oldRowBytes (:86–88); transfer uses parent object count/bytes (:89–91); frontier completion uses rowContextBytes (:93–94). These forecasts do not refund previous reads. Actual scalar values and each component vector are not printed. |\n| 5. Adaptive/fixed selection setup and snapshot versus standalone context work | Driver strategy/context selection is at `archive-driver.ts:395–422`; snapshot preparation pays at `archive-row.ts:419–462`; adaptive setup pays at `archive-adaptive.ts:57–77`. | Adaptive final-candidate handoff versus conservative setup is selected at :153–154. Its setup vector enters the request (`archive-finish-cost.ts:97–99`). Earlier layout/preparation is already spent. Actual snapshot consumption and setup/selection vectors are not printed. |\n\nThe refused quote's source-defined components are, separately: **setup + inventory + shape.input + publication + selectionReservation + selection + body + patch + commit + conditional appendEdges + conditional append + transfer + rows + frontier** (`archive-finish-cost.ts:97–99`). Publication covers public source/anchor identities and related checks (:47–70); patch/body/commit cover journal output (:71–85); transfer/rows/frontier cover the future send and retained progress (:86–94). `sourceLookups` is an observed subset of publication, not an additional term (:100–120).\n\n**No retained numeric component breakdown exists for either refused quote.** The ordinary supplied-budget observation explicitly prints `quoteCalls:0`, `firstQuote:null`, `selectedQuote:null`, `lastCompleteQuote:null`, `debitAttribution:'unavailable'`, and incomplete flags. Its separately printed refusal still supplies the complete aggregate request and six-axis comparison above. This report does not infer per-part totals, repeated-byte amounts, a sufficient cap, or minimum caps from the aggregate.\n\nSpecific missing numbers for a later planner assignment, only if needed: (a) for the exact child seq 1 and Grow seq 0 refused quotes, each of the named finish-component six-axis vectors and its scalar inputs; (b) if ARC-1 needs to decide duplicate work, operation/site-specific nodes and inputWork debits tied to the same scope reference or immutable bytes, including settlement; (c) for any confirmed Base pass Hugh asks about, its actual successful finish quote and used vector immediately before it. Ordinary output supplies none of these. No new observer or run is proposed here.\n\n## Actual main 863: these two cases are absent\n\nAt `863ca6b2ee23c528af97b352165092c556ca35f9`, `archive-installed.test.ts:3` selects only fixture, Grow, Grow activation warm, Grow activation evicted, Grow publication, Grow failed-claim, Grow base, and Grow Room A shape. It selects neither shared Base nor shared Grow. The shape scenario registers the old-R17 title.\n\nThe accepted LC1 full-gate evidence at faece658 records **eight distinct final case identities**, all passed, for this owner, with module duration **52,585 ms**. It contains neither shared target. The owner, fixture, adaptive source and finish forecast have an empty Git diff from faece658 to main863. Thus Base-child-seq1 and shared-Grow-producer-seq0 decisions/used vectors on main are **not applicable: those cases do not exist in that owner**. They are not unprinted measurements of cases that ran. Repeating the unchanged main owner cannot produce them, so this report requests no such run.\n\n## Retained evidence\n\nAll paths below are under `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/`.\n\n| Record | Path | SHA-256 / qualification |\n|---|---|---|\n| Original END755 ordinary stdout | `2026-11-14-ae1-integrated-development-attempt1/12-native.stdout.log` | `058468eec5339bb0f99c9f14bcb4103ba1cce1e5ac72a1b39c25bbf250ca5270`; Native 74 = 69 pass / 5 fail, 52.71390875 s |\n| Exact-ca1 ordinary replay stdout | `2026-11-14-ae1-end755-replay-attempt1/owner.stdout.log` | `dfcb6108e44194899d328c1d54a9ed70f033ec4e64fc68c1c526476702a7ba8d`; owner 12 = 8 pass / 4 fail, exit 1, 54.537679667 s |\n| Replay actual case report | `2026-11-14-ae1-end755-replay-attempt1/owner.report.json` | `d142f4233374e43b1e95be643e50df0dd47120ed0f45e4ce7c28383806e1ec5b` |\n| Replay result | `2026-11-14-ae1-end755-replay-attempt1/result.json` | `950ae6a41282f519472e4acd21c0694e13b0bde95acce64b9e0df8991f605ddf` |\n| Main's accepted LC1 native case records | `2026-11-14-lc1-full-gate-attempt1/stage-logs/test-evidence/native.jsonl` | `efef58f0cc0593accba412e7937d63b99467a74b938fc8b81dcb70ee7df6e0c1`; use `record:case, source:final` to avoid counting duplicate result/final records |\n| Main's LC1 gate | `2026-11-14-lc1-full-gate-attempt1/result.json` and `gate.log` | END1186e84b; exit 0, 870.297345083 s. Gate log SHA `0ad7621fac3b17b864702b773561bc0bd6a41f968f49997264010d080a2ab268` |\n\nThe historical failures, incorrect diagnostic target selection, and accepted source-attribution correction remain preserved separately. This report changes no verdict and makes no AE-1 fit or acceptance claim.\n\n\nRoot verification: full report read; the Grow aggregate refusal and all four faece658-to-main source correspondences were independently checked. Eight final main-corresponding case records all passed and contain neither shared target. No main rerun can measure these absent target cases, so their main decisions/vectors are N/A, not missing unobserved runs. Durable retained-capacity-numbers.md SHA-256 b8f04cb5d90fbc1e45dcf85e238db4730af9d3b8044eeac4810bcd0c058a46a9. C3's authorized local browser route owns the executor; no new AE1 execution occurred.","body":{"evidence_dir":"/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-14-ae1-end755-replay-attempt1","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c4f1b4edb3073a7fe912ae65e26b88558d75b125, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cbbf87e88f0c0a4ff683c721c504c02ca2247ed4 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:049f20c5be4bf9b931e2a3b17c58ee482654b6d4, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06237ac0edb5e6d93d5fe9c9f9bb841c01fbfb55, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0b524b76231732ccddc1efbc5386b8bb808edf80, git:sha1:589bca9